+                  <h4>About the Role</h4>
                   <p>
-                    Full job description coming soon. Email us directly and
-                    the team can walk you through the role in the meantime.
+                    V-Chip is seeking a hands-on Lead Design Verification
+                    Engineer to lead pre-silicon verification of complex
+                    semiconductor IP, subsystems, and SoC designs. You will
+                    define verification strategies, guide execution, and
+                    collaborate with multidisciplinary engineering teams to
+                    deliver robust, production-ready silicon.
                   </p>
+                  <h4>Responsibilities</h4>
+                  <ul>
+                    <li>
+                      Own the verification strategy, methodology, schedule,
+                      and sign-off criteria for assigned IP, subsystem, or
+                      full-chip projects
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Develop comprehensive, requirements-driven verification
+                      plans and ensure traceability from specifications to
+                      tests and coverage
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Architect and develop reusable SystemVerilog/UVM
+                      verification environments, including testbenches,
+                      sequences, agents, scoreboards, reference models,
+                      assertions, and coverage models
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Lead constrained-random, directed, assertion-based,
+                      and coverage-driven verification activities
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Execute and debug RTL and gate-level simulations,
+                      regressions, and failing test cases
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Drive verification closure by analysing functional and
+                      code coverage, identifying gaps, and coordinating
+                      corrective actions
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Review design specifications and RTL implementations
+                      to identify functional, integration, and verification
+                      risks early
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Collaborate closely with architects, RTL designers,
+                      software engineers, physical design engineers, DFT
+                      engineers, and external IP providers
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Support design integration, logic synthesis, linting,
+                      clock-domain crossing checks, reset-domain checks, and
+                      formal equivalence activities where required
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Establish verification best practices, reusable
+                      infrastructure, automation, and quality metrics across
+                      projects
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Provide technical leadership, conduct reviews, mentor
+                      junior engineers, and support project planning and
+                      resource estimation
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Communicate verification status, risks, dependencies,
+                      and sign-off readiness clearly to project stakeholders
+                    </li>
+                  </ul>
+                  <h4>Qualifications</h4>
+                  <ul>
+                    <li>
+                      Bachelor's or Master's degree in Electrical
+                      Engineering, Electronics Engineering, Computer
+                      Engineering, or a related discipline
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      At least 7 years of relevant experience in ASIC, SoC,
+                      FPGA, or IP-level functional verification, including
+                      technical leadership responsibilities
+                    </li>
+                    <li>Strong hands-on experience with SystemVerilog and UVM</li>
+                    <li>
+                      Proven experience developing verification plans and
+                      coverage-driven verification environments from the
+                      ground up
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Solid understanding of constrained-random
+                      verification, functional coverage, code coverage,
+                      assertions, and verification closure
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Strong debugging skills across testbench, RTL,
+                      waveform, protocol, and system-level failures
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Experience with industry-standard simulation and
+                      verification tools from Cadence, Siemens EDA, or
+                      Synopsys
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Familiarity with common interfaces and protocols such
+                      as AMBA AXI/AHB/APB, PCIe, Ethernet, DDR, USB, or other
+                      high-speed interfaces
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Good understanding of digital design concepts, SoC
+                      architectures, clock and reset structures, and
+                      hardware/software interactions
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Working knowledge of scripting or programming
+                      languages such as Python, Perl, Tcl, C, or C++
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Strong communication, problem-solving, technical
+                      leadership, and cross-functional collaboration skills
+                    </li>
+                  </ul>
+                  <h4>Preferred Experience</h4>
+                  <ul>
+                    <li>
+                      Verification of complex SoCs, processor-based systems,
+                      high-speed interfaces, or reusable semiconductor IP
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Formal verification, emulation, FPGA prototyping,
+                      low-power verification, or performance verification
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Gate-level simulation, logic synthesis, lint, CDC/RDC
+                      analysis, and equivalence checking
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Regression automation, continuous integration,
+                      version-control workflows, and verification
+                      productivity tools
+                    </li>
+                    <li>
+                      Experience mentoring engineers or leading a
+                      verification team through project sign-off
+                    </li>
+                  </ul>
